{
  "info": {
    "name": "Monster Raid Service (Team 14)",
    "description": "Cooperative guild raids against a shared monster.\n\nOwner: Dackohn. Port: 8086 (reached through the gateway on 8080).\n\nEverything goes through the API Gateway (`{{gatewayUrl}}`, port 8080): players log in at User Management through it, and the gateway verifies their token and forwards requests with `X-User-Id` + `X-Gateway-Key` instead. The service itself accepts nothing else - the `... without the gateway` request shows the 401. Each run registers new players (`{{runId}}`), so it can be run repeatedly.\n\nPackage Registry creates the raid through the Message Broker (`{{brokerUrl}}`, port 8090), as it does in the stack: POST /raids is a service-only endpoint the gateway no longer forwards. Set {{packageRegistryServiceKey}} to PACKAGE_REGISTRY_MONSTER_RAID_SERVICE_KEY and {{brokerKey}} to BROKER_KEY from .env (newman: `--env-var packageRegistryServiceKey=<key> --env-var brokerKey=<key>`).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "gatewayUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "raidUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8086"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "Secret123!"
    },
    {
      "key": "runId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "ownerToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "ownerId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "outsiderToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "outsiderId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "guildId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "tamagotchiId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "raidId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "wsUrl",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "packageRegistryServiceKey",
      "value": "change_me"
    },
    {
      "key": "brokerUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8090"
    },
    {
      "key": "brokerKey",
      "value": "change_me"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "monster-raid-service is up behind the gateway",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Every run starts here with a new runId, so each run registers new players.",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('runId', String(Date.now()));"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
              "pm.test('monster-raid-service is ok', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.json().services['monster-raid-service'].status).to.eql('ok'); });"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gatewayUrl}}/health/services",
          "host": [
            "{{gatewayUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "health",
            "services"
          ]
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Status of one replica (Lab 3)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('names the service and the replica', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('ok');",
              "    pm.expect(body.service).to.eql('monster-raid-service');",
              "    pm.expect(body.instanceId).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "    pm.expect(body.version).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "});",
              "pm.test('reports its load', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(body.uptimeSeconds).to.be.a('number');",
              "    pm.expect(body.inFlightRequests).to.be.a('number');",
              "    pm.expect(body.maxConcurrentRequests).to.be.a('number').and.above(0);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{raidUrl}}/health",
          "host": [
            "{{raidUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "health"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Lab 3 status endpoint, read directly through ws-proxy (port 8086), which hands the request to one replica. Public and outside the request limits: it answers 200 even when the replica is saturated."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Every replica is up (Lab 3)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const svc = pm.response.json().services['monster-raid-service'];",
              "pm.test('the gateway routes to several replicas', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(svc.instances).to.be.an('array');",
              "    pm.expect(svc.instances.length).to.be.at.least(2);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('every replica answers its health check', () => {",
              "    svc.instances.forEach((i) => pm.expect(i.status, i.url).to.eql('ok'));",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gatewayUrl}}/health/services",
          "host": [
            "{{gatewayUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "health",
            "services"
          ]
        },
        "description": "The gateway probes every replica it routes to, from the lists it reads from Service Discovery."
      },
      "response": []
    },
