    {
      "name": "Live raid (WebSocket)",
      "item": [],
      "description": "Postman's collection format can't store WebSocket requests, so create it in the app:\n\n1. Run the collection up to `Negotiate the live raid socket`; it saves the URL with a one-time ticket into {{wsUrl}}.\n2. New -> WebSocket, URL {{wsUrl}} (save it in this collection), Connect within 60 s. You get { \"event\": \"raid\", \"data\": <the raid> }.\n3. Run the two attacks: each arrives as { \"event\": \"attack\", ... }, then { \"event\": \"completed\", ... } and the socket closes (1000).\n\nOnly participants may watch; anyone else, or a reused ticket, is closed with 1008."
    }
